# Raw agent transcripts, and the v1 per-run stats beside them
# (runs/stats = stats_raw_store in ../config/runtime.conf — the records CR-031
# backfilled this journal's economics from). Transcripts are private by default
# at every capture preset (ADR-0005 Decision 2); publishing one is a separate
# escalation needing two independent opt-ins. Anchored so it matches this
# directory only — an unanchored "runs/" matches at any depth and silently
# swept up stats/runs/ as well.
/runs/

# Left unanchored deliberately: it was, and changing that would alter what is
# publishable without a decision. Nothing in src/agentmarshal writes here; the
# directory holds a "runner" entry left by operator tooling. Scratch either way.
tmp/

# Any .log at any depth in the journal: tool output, not evidence. Nothing in
# the record model produces one, so a .log here is a byproduct of running
# something and belongs to the machine that ran it.
*.log

# stats_store (../config/runtime.conf): where am-lead-stats --write emits
# v1-schema per-run records so the lead channel shows up in the legacy summary.
# Local working data, not evidence — the journal's own session records are the
# supported economics and are published with the rest of the journal. Scoped to
# this path alone: evaluation_store (stats/evaluations) was never ignored, and
# its publication status is not this rule's to decide.
/stats/runs/
